+
+## Limitations & Known Issues
+None. All reachable limitations were resolved.
+
+Design facts and pre-existing upstream behaviour (not port work):
+- No upstream test suite exists; validation is differential against the x64 build.
+- The `sleep & kill -INT $!` race in `src/jobs.c:902-904` is pre-existing
+  upstream and reproduces on x64 (18/100 x64, 12/100 ARM64).
+- The `GLOB_ALTDIRFUNC` redefinition warning (`src/expand.c:1476` vs
+  `src/system.h:146`) appears on both architectures.
+- Performance residual on interpreter loops (1.00-1.20x vs emulated x64): the
+  compiler default tune is cortex-a53 and the runtime versions differ.
+  Optimization was skipped by request.
+- The MSYS2 recipe builds aarch64 at `-O1` because of toolchain issue #38. With
+  the current cross GCC 17.0.0 20260828, `-O2` builds dash cleanly, so that
+  workaround may no longer be needed for this package.
+
+## Reverting / Coexistence
+The x64 build is unchanged. A native build that does not set `CC_FOR_BUILD`
+behaves exactly as before. To build x64, use `main` or omit `--build`/`--host`.
